    "review.butterfly-iq.faq.3.answer.the.device.works.without.a.subscription.for.basic.": "The device works without a subscription for basic imaging and local storage on your smartphone or tablet. However, the $49/month subscription unlocks crucial features including cloud storage, AI-powered measurements, telemedicine capabilities, advanced imaging modes, and continuous software updates. Most users find the subscription essential for professional use, especially for cloud archiving and AI assistance. The annual plan at $420/year saves 30% compared to monthly billing.",
    "review.butterfly-iq.faq.4.question.what.devices.are.compatible.with.butterfly.iq": "What devices are compatible with Butterfly iQ?",
    "review.butterfly-iq.faq.4.answer.butterfly.iq.connects.via.usb.c.to.compatible.ios.": "Butterfly iQ connects via USB-C to compatible iOS and Android devices. For iOS, it requires iPhone 8 or newer and iPad (5th generation or newer) running iOS 13 or later. For Android, it requires devices with USB-C ports running Android 9 or newer. The Butterfly iQ app is free to download. The device includes an adapter for older Lightning port iPhones. Check the Butterfly Network website for the most current compatibility list.",
    "review.butterfly-iq.faq.5.question.can.butterfly.iq.integrate.with.our.ehr.system": "Can Butterfly iQ integrate with our EHR system?",
    "review.butterfly-iq.faq.5.answer.yes.butterfly.iq.supports.dicom.export.and.integr": "Yes, Butterfly iQ supports DICOM export and integrates with major EHR systems including Epic, Cerner, and others. Images can be exported directly to PACS systems or sent via secure links. Enterprise customers receive dedicated integration support and custom workflows. The cloud platform also provides APIs for custom integrations. All data transmission is HIPAA-compliant with end-to-end encryption.",
